      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have no idea why the test does not run at presubmit, and why we need a property to pass some AVRCP tests, could this be manual PTS testing?\n\nIn this case the only thing I could think of that would explain why we would skip the \"root\" folder created by Android is that it will return not a list of media but a list of browsable folders and PTS might want to play one of the folder items it received: it sends browsing event, then tries to play one item it received -\u003e as we return a media folder and not a media in root it might fail the test so we select directly a browsable player and fetch its content.\n\nIf this fix works, I\u0027m not sure why we would need the property though as it looks similar to what happens without it.\n\n@ruinali@amazon.com is the test passing without the property set (or without the conditions in the methods you are modifying)?\n\n@wescande@google.com you may want to contact whoever made the modification for the PTS tests and ask them why this has been done like that because I won\u0027t have a final answer here (can\u0027t run the tests locally right now). :)",
